{"name":"Flowering Raspberry","hex":"#a16c94","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"flowering","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of flower"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The period of time during which a plant is in flower.","The period of time during which someone or something is at its peak."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/flowering"},{"term":"raspberry","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The plant Rubus idaeus.","Any of many other (but not all) species in the genus Rubus."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the flavor/flavour of raspberries.","Of a dark pinkish red."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raspberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rubus odoratus","blocks":[{"text":"Rubus odoratus, the purple-flowered raspberry, flowering raspberry, or Virginia raspberry, is a species of Rubus native to eastern North America. It is sometimes referred to as thimbleberry, a name more commonly associated with the North American R. parviflorus."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Rubus-odoratus-flower.JPG/330px-Rubus-odoratus-flower.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rubus_odoratus"},{"title":"Flower","blocks":[{"text":"Flowers, also known as blossoms and blooms, are the reproductive structures of flowering plants. Typically, they are structured in four circular levels around the end of a stalk. These include: sepals, which are modified leaves that support the flower; petals, often designed to attract pollinators; male stamens, where pollen is presented; and female gynoecia, where pollen is received and its movement is facilitated to the egg. When flowers are arranged in a group, they are known collectively as an inflorescence."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg/330px-Magnolia_grandiflora_-_flower_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flower"},{"title":"Raspberry","blocks":[{"text":"The raspberry is the edible fruit of several plant species in the genus Rubus of the rose family, most of which are in the subgenus Idaeobatus. The name also applies to these plants themselves. Raspberries are perennial with woody stems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Raspberry_-_halved_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg/330px-Raspberry_-_halved_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raspberry"},{"title":"Raspberry (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Raspberry is a color that resembles the color of raspberries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Raspberry_-_whole_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg/330px-Raspberry_-_whole_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raspberry_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Rubus_odoratus_2016-05-09_9979.jpg/500px-Rubus_odoratus_2016-05-09_9979.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Rubus_odoratus_2016-05-09_9979.jpg/960px-Rubus_odoratus_2016-05-09_9979.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Rubus_odoratus_2016-05-09_9979.jpg/500px-Rubus_odoratus_2016-05-09_9979.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARubus_odoratus_2016-05-09_9979.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Rubus_odoratus_2017-05-23_0538.jpg/500px-Rubus_odoratus_2017-05-23_0538.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.or